    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Trea Turner** (78.26) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.75) anchoring the offense. Both benefit significantly from a prime matchup against Sugano; the combination of favorable park factors and high-leverage order placement yields an elite environment for our top-of-the-order threats. **Yordan Alvarez** (72.28) remains a must-start despite the left-on-left disadvantage against Abbott, as his elite xwOBA (0.428) consistently overcomes platoon headwinds. Meanwhile, **Junior Caminero** (63.50) and **Dillon Dingler** (60.86) provide the necessary depth to maintain our efficiency floor, with **Dillon Dingler** specifically benefiting from a high-upside platoon edge against the southpaw Cameron. \n\nStrategic allocation in our scarcity-driven categories is highlighted by the decision to play **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (52.12). While facing an elite arm like deGrom is undeniably daunting, the 14% boost from a favorable platoon matchup and his high sprint speed keep him in the lineup, as his potential to steal bases remains a critical component of our 5x5 strategy. On the bench, **Chase Meidroth** (37.95) was the closest candidate to cracking the lineup, but a sharp negative variance in SP skill against Logan Gilbert pushed his daily score below our 40.0 floor, making him a necessary sit to preserve our game caps. Be advised that **Dillon Dingler**, **Colt Keith**, and **Carson Benge** are currently operating under \"Lineup Pending\" status; should their actual batting positions fluctuate downward, we will need to monitor their efficiency scores closely to ensure we aren't wasting at-bats in low-leverage spots.",
